**Unit-test harness constraint (drives the whole TDD plan).** `package.json:39`: `"test:unit": "node --import tsx --test \"plugins/**/*.test.ts\" \"src/**/*.test.ts\""`. There is no vitest, no jsdom test runner, no `@testing-library`. Only `*.test.ts` (never `.tsx`) under `src/` runs, under plain `node --test` + `tsx`. The single existing unit spec is `src/components/QuestionnaireV2/structured/pluginRegistry.test.ts` (126 lines) and it documents the boundary explicitly at `pluginRegistry.test.ts:98-100`:

> `registry.ts` pulls in every structured definition's real component tree (CSS, UI libs) and is exercised via the questionnaire fill/structured Playwright specs instead.

**Consequence for Phase 1:** every new unit-testable primitive must live in a `.ts` module that imports **nothing from React, no `.tsx`, and not `registry.ts`**. Concretely: the edit-log algebra, the projection function, and the contract discriminator must be their own leaf modules (`structured/core/edits.ts`, `structured/core/projectRows.ts`, `structured/contract.ts`), with `useStructuredRows.ts` (React) as a thin wrapper over them. That is the only way Phase 1 gets real TDD instead of Playwright-only coverage.

